Chapter: NarratorTest

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Works chapter Annotation
  cites Works chapter Narrator

 The Narrator folds a definition's annotations into a narration block,
 and the fold is SELECTIVE: Rationale, Discovery and Doctrine narrate,
 while Invariant, Warning and Todo do not. That selection is the whole
 behaviour worth pinning, and it is exactly what the old body could not
 see -- it created one Annotation, printed its kind, and narrated
 nothing, so it passed with nothing behind it.

 So this feeds one annotation of every kind and asserts both halves:
 the three that narrate appear in the formatted output, and the three
 that do not are absent.

 The selection is enforced TWICE and in series -- `fold-narration`
 guards on `is-narration-kind`, and `add-narration-line` then dispatches
 on the kind and returns the block untouched for Invariant, Warning and
 Todo. So this pins the composite property rather than either site, and
 removing one guard alone changes nothing. Measured: with both removed,
 line-count goes to 4 and `warning` flips to yes. Do not read a green
 here as evidence that a particular guard is live.

Section: Fixtures

  nt-target : AnnotationTarget
  nt-target = make-target "Narrator" "tell-story"

  nt-ann : AnnotationKind, Text -> Annotation
  nt-ann (k) (body) = create-annotation nt-target k "fester" body 100

  nt-annotations : List Annotation
  nt-annotations = [
    nt-ann Rationale "because the prose is load-bearing",
    nt-ann Discovery "the fold turned out to be selective",
    nt-ann Doctrine "narration is not documentation",
    nt-ann Invariant "the balance is never negative",
    nt-ann Warning "this sits on a hot path",
    nt-ann Todo "revisit after the migration"
  ]

Section: Helpers

 The formatted narration is threaded as a parameter rather than read
 from a top-level constant. A constant is rebuilt at every mention, so
 reading one seven times would run format-narration seven times.

  nt-has : Text, Text -> Text
  nt-has (haystack) (needle) =
    if text-contains haystack needle then "yes" else "no"

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let anns = nt-annotations
    in let block = fold-narration anns 0 (list-length anns) (empty-narration nt-target)
    in let out = format-narration block
    in act
      print-line-uni ("target=" & target-key nt-target)
      print-line-uni ("lines=" & show (block.line-count))
      print-line-uni ("rationale=" & nt-has out "load-bearing")
      print-line-uni ("discovery=" & nt-has out "selective")
      print-line-uni ("doctrine=" & nt-has out "not documentation")
      print-line-uni ("invariant=" & nt-has out "never negative")
      print-line-uni ("warning=" & nt-has out "hot path")
      print-line-uni ("todo=" & nt-has out "after the migration")
    end
